        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Bool From A Pattern"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "matches!(v, Some(x) if x > 3) // -> bool",
            "xs.iter().filter(|v| matches!(v, Ok(_)))",
            "assert!(matches!(e, Event::Close));"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Sharp Edges",
          "items": [
            "`if let` with a guard is not allowed",
            "let-chains (`if let Some(x) = a && x > 3`): edition 2024 only",
            "Not available in edition 2021",
            "`if let Ok(_) = r` throws the error away silently"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Shadowing Idiom",
          "text": "`if let Some(opt) = opt { .. }` reuses the name on purpose — inside the block, `opt` is the unwrapped value, and there is nothing left to confuse it with."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Boundary One-Liner"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let port = env::var(\"PORT\").ok()",
            "    .and_then(|s| s.parse().ok())",
            "    .unwrap_or(8080);"
          ],
          "note": "Result → Option → value"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No `unwrap` on user input",
            "No bare `_` arm in enums you own",
            "Errors carry context via `map_err`"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        }
